  "datePublished": "2026-02",
  "abstract": "Five-phase systematic localization study testing EFC against Planck 2018 CMB likelihoods, DESI 2024 BAO, SDSS DR12 BAO, and Pantheon+ supernovae. Background sector is observationally empty (α → 0). Perturbation sector survives within a narrow slip window (μ ∈ [0.93, 0.96], Σ ∈ [1.03, 1.07]). The (μ, Σ) valley is degenerate with the A_L anomaly (cos = 0.93), but fσ₈ data independently confirm μ < 1 at > 2σ, breaking the degeneracy. A relativistic perturbation theory producing gravitational slip (η ≠ 1) is required.",
